- **Required interface:**
  - `int HeifContext::Image::get_luma_bits_per_pixel() const;`
  - `int HeifContext::Image::get_chroma_bits_per_pixel() const;`

  Both are declared in `libheif/heif_context.h` and called by the `heif.cc` C entry points `heif_image_handle_get_luma_bits_per_pixel` / `heif_image_handle_get_chroma_bits_per_pixel`, which return the values unchanged. The derived-item resolution they use is a private member of the same class whose only call sites lie inside this region, so its name, signature and decomposition are not required.
- **Observable behavior:** Resolves a logical image'"'"'s bit depth through the item holding its codec configuration: items of type `grid`, `iden`, or `iovl` resolve through the first of their `dimg` item references, repeating until an item of a non-derived type is reached; any other item type resolves to itself. The result is the codec-configuration bit depth of the resolved item, queried from the retained file model.
- **Inputs:** The image'"'"'s item ID and owning context; the file model'"'"'s item-type query, item-reference box, and the `dimg` reference list for the item.
- **Outputs and errors:** Each getter returns one `int` bit depth (luma/chroma respectively). No errors are emitted. Both complete for every image of a successfully read file; the value for a derived image for which the file records no item references is left open.
- **Side effects and interactions:** None — const, read-only; consumes the retained `HeifFile` item-type and iref-box accessors, the retained `Box_iref` reference query with the `dimg` four-character code, and the `HeifFile` configuration bit-depth queries.
- **Required sequencing and state:** Resolution precedes the configuration query; the query runs on the resolved item ID, not the original one.
- **Region boundary:** Self-contained: the range spans three whole top-level definitions; the retained text above ends with the previous definition'"'"'s closing brace and the retained text below opens a new definition, so nothing must be left open or closed, and no name defined here is referenced by the retained text below.
