- **Observable behavior:** Declares the logical image model — the context, its nested images, and metadata records. Each inline getter returns what the corresponding setter last wrote. `ImageMetadata` carries one metadata block; `heif.cc`'"'"'s metadata entry points read all four of its members by name. Both classes derive from `ErrorBuffer` so `heif.cc` can report errors through them.
- **Inputs:** Setter/constructor arguments: integer resolutions, item IDs, flags, shared pointers to images/metadata/color profiles, `heif_depth_representation_info`; the declared non-inline members take the C API types from `heif.h`, `heif_plugin.h`, and `bitstream.h`.
- **Outputs and errors:** Getters return the stored state (`int`, `bool`, `heif_item_id`, shared pointers, vectors, `const heif_depth_representation_info&`). Inline members emit no errors; non-inline members return `Error` per `heif_context.cc`.
- **Side effects and interactions:** Setters mutate the state the getters expose; `add_thumbnail`/`add_metadata` preserve insertion order, which `heif.cc`'"'"'s enumeration entry points expose; `set_depth_representation_info` also sets the presence flag.
- **Required sequencing and state:** A newly constructed `Image` reports zero sizes, false flags, absent depth info, and empty lists through the declared default initializers until setters run (`heif_context.cc`'"'"'s constructor relies on this). `is_primary_image_set()` reflects primary-image presence.
