```
- **Required interface:** `async def check_allowed(self, username, auth_model)` — public async method on `GlobusOAuthenticator`, overriding `oauthenticator.oauth2.OAuthenticator.check_allowed`. Reached during the authentication flow by the installed JupyterHub'"'"'s `get_authenticated_user` machinery (the call ordering and gating belong to that machinery), and awaited directly by the project'"'"'s tests as `authenticator.check_allowed(username, auth_model)`, including calls where `auth_model` is None. Calls `super().check_allowed(username, auth_model)` on the retained base class.
- **Observable behavior:** Decides whether an authenticated user is allowed, combining an identity-provider domain comparison, the base allowance decision, and Globus-group membership.
- **Inputs:** `username` — a normalized username string. `auth_model` — dict or None; when a dict, `auth_model["auth_state"]` holds the userinfo dict under `self.user_auth_state_key` (containing an entry named by `self.username_claim`) and a `"globus_groups"` list of group ids. Traits read: `identity_provider`, `username_claim`, `allowed_globus_groups`, `user_auth_state_key`.
- **Outputs and errors:** `check_allowed` returns a bool. An authenticated account whose domain does not match a configured `identity_provider` is refused with `tornado.web.HTTPError(403, message)` where message is `This site is restricted to {identity_provider} accounts. Link your account at app.globus.org/account.` with the configured `identity_provider` value interpolated; the exception propagates to the caller.
- **Side effects and interactions:** Logs a warning with the same text as the raised 403 message on a domain mismatch, and a warning naming the username and stating they are not in an allowed Globus Group when group membership does not match. Reads auth state populated by `update_auth_model`; defers the standard allowance decision to the base `check_allowed`.
- **Required sequencing and state:** `check_allowed` in order: (1) if `auth_model` is None, return True; (2) return True when the base `check_allowed` returns True; (3) when `allowed_globus_groups` is non-empty, return True when it intersects `auth_state["globus_groups"]`, otherwise log the group warning; (4) return False. When `identity_provider` is set, an authenticated account whose domain — everything after the first `'"'"'@'"'"'` in the value of the `username_claim` entry of the userinfo dict — differs from `identity_provider` is refused: the warning is logged and the 403 raised. No mutation of `auth_model`.
- **Region boundary:** Self-contained — the range spans the entire method declaration. The retained text above ends the preceding `_fetch_users_groups` method and the retained text below starts `async def update_auth_model`; the replacement supplies the complete `check_allowed` method at class-body indentation, together with any further class members it needs, and leaves nothing open.
