- **Side effects and interactions:** Reads `im`'"'"'s truecolor pixel buffer; allocates and frees a working pixel buffer; invokes libwebp to encode; writes bytes via the IO sink; frees the working buffers.
- **Required sequencing and state:** Reject a `NULL` image (return 1); reject a non-truecolor image (`gd_error` + return 1); map `quality == -1` to the default; compute the working-buffer size from the image dimensions and allocate it, returning 1 on failure; build the RGBA buffer from the image'"'"'s pixels and alpha; encode via libwebp; if no bytes are produced (`gd_error` + return 1), otherwise write the bytes; free the working buffers; return the status.
- **Region boundary:** Self-contained (a whole function definition, opening `static int _gdImageWebpCtx(...)` through its closing brace). It sits within the `#ifdef HAVE_LIBWEBP` block; retained wrappers below the region reference the name `_gdImageWebpCtx`, so the replacement must define a function with that exact name and signature.
