  gdPutBuf                   int (const void *, int, gdIOCtx *)                       [gd_io.c / gd_io.h]

  The IO-sink contract (gd_io.h / gd_io.c) callers depend on:

  gdIOCtx                    struct with function-pointer members putBuf, putC,
                             getBuf, getC, seek, tell, gd_free (typedef
                             gdIOCtx *gdIOCtxPtr)
  gdNewDynamicCtx            gdIOCtx * (int initial, void *...) — constructs an
                             in-memory dynamic sink
  gdDPExtractData            void * (gdIOCtx *, int *size) — extracts accumulated bytes

## Called as
  BMP encoder, Ctx form (caller builds an in-memory sink and passes the
  produced bytes to the BMP decoder):
      gdIOCtx *out = gdNewDynamicCtx(2048, NULL);
      gdImageBmpCtx(im, out, compression);
      void *data = gdDPExtractData(out, &sz);
      out->gd_free(out);
      gdImageCreateFromBmpPtr(sz, data);
      gdFree(data);
    im           — 1st positional; gdImagePtr (a palette image built with
                   gdImageCreate / gdImageColorAllocate / gdImageSetPixel)
    out          — 2nd positional; gdIOCtxPtr, a caller-supplied sink
    compression  — 3rd positional; an int

  WebP encoder, Ctx form:
      gdIOCtx *out = gdNewDynamicCtx(2048, NULL);
      gdImageWebpCtx(im, out, quantization);
      void *data = gdDPExtractData(out, &sz);
      out->gd_free(out);
      gdImageCreateFromWebpPtr(sz, data);
      gdFree(data);
    im            — 1st positional; gdImagePtr (a truecolor image built with
                    gdImageCreateTrueColor / gdTrueColor / gdImageSetPixel)
    out           — 2nd positional; gdIOCtxPtr, a caller-supplied sink
    quantization  — 3rd positional; an int

  BMP encoder, Ptr form:
      void *data = gdImageBmpPtr(im, &sz, compression);
      gdImageCreateFromBmpPtr(sz, data);
      gdFree(data);
    im           — 1st positional; gdImagePtr
    &sz          — 2nd positional; int * (out-param for encoded byte count)
    compression  — 3rd positional; an int

  WebP encoder, Ptr form:
      void *data = gdImageWebpPtr(im, &sz);
      gdImageCreateFromWebpPtr(sz, data);
      gdFree(data);
    im   — 1st positional; gdImagePtr
    &sz  — 2nd positional; int * (out-param for encoded byte count)

  BMP encoder, FILE form (caller opens a path and reopens it for reading):
      FILE *fp = fopen(path, "wb");
      gdImageBmp(im, fp, compression);
      fclose(fp);
      fp = fopen(path, "rb");
      gdImageCreateFromBmp(fp);
      fclose(fp);
    im           — 1st positional; gdImagePtr
    fp           — 2nd positional; FILE * (opened by the caller)
    compression  — 3rd positional; an int

  Error channel (a second caller installs a handler before driving the same
  encoder entry points; the sink below is a caller-constructed gdIOCtx whose
  putBuf/putC/seek/tell/gd_free members the caller fills in):
      gdSetErrorMethod(capture_error);   /* capture_error: void(*)(int, const char *, va_list) */
      gdImageBmpCtx(im, (gdIOCtx *)&sink, compression);
      gdImageWebpCtx(im, (gdIOCtx *)&sink, quantization);

