### pkg/downloader/uri.go
Masked section 1:
```
- **Required interface:** `func GetURI(url string, f func(url string, i []byte) error) error` — exported, package-level. Reached by `pkg/gallery.GetGalleryConfigFromURL`, `pkg/gallery.getGalleryModels`/reference-resolution, `embedded.GetRemoteLibraryShorteners`, and `core/http/app_test.go`, each passing a callback `func(url string, i []byte) error`. The callback'"'"'s first argument is consumed by callers (the resolved URL string), so the URL handed to `f` is part of the contract.
- **Observable behavior:** Fetches the content addressed by `url` and invokes `f` with the URL string and the raw bytes. The input `url` is first passed through `ConvertURL`. If the resolved URL has the `file://` prefix, the prefix is stripped and symbolic links on the resulting local path are resolved; on the path where the read proceeds, the file is read and `f` is called with the **original** `url` (the `file://` form) and the file'"'"'s bytes. Otherwise an HTTP GET is performed against the resolved URL, the response body is read in full, and `f` is called with the **resolved** URL and the body bytes.
- **Inputs:** `url` (string), `f` (callback `(url string, i []byte) error`).
- **Outputs and errors:** Returns `nil` when `f` returns `nil` and no fetch error occurred; otherwise an error — among them the ones from URL conversion, symbolic-link resolution, the file read, the HTTP request, the body read, and `f`. The exact error type/wording is not externally consumed.
- **Side effects and interactions:** For non-`file://` URLs issues a network HTTP GET and reads the response body; for `file://` URLs reads the local filesystem (resolving symlinks). Writes no files. Depends on `ConvertURL` (r1) for URL normalization.
- **Required sequencing and state:** URL conversion happens before fetch dispatch; the `file://` branch resolves symlinks before reading; the HTTP branch closes the response body after reading. The callback is invoked exactly once with bytes already in hand.
- **Region boundary:** Self-contained — the range spans the whole `GetURI` declaration, beginning at its `func` line and ending at its closing brace. No surrounding retained text is left open or unclosed by this region.
```

Masked section 2:
```
- **Required interface:** `func ConvertURL(s string) string` — exported, package-level. Reached by `core/config.BackendConfig` (`MMProjFileName`, `IsMMProjURL`, `IsModelURL`, `ModelFileName`) and `core/config.BackendConfigLoader` (model/mmproj URL computation); also called internally by `GetURI` (r0) and `DownloadFile` (r2).
- **Observable behavior:** Returns a canonical URL string derived from `s`: `github://org/project/sub/path[@branch]` and `github:org/project/sub/path[@branch]` map to `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/org/project/branch/sub/path` (branch defaulting to `main` when no `@branch` is present); `huggingface://owner/repo/file[@branch]` maps to `https://huggingface.co/owner/repo/resolve/branch/file` (branch defaulting to `main`). Any other input is returned unchanged.
- **Inputs:** `s` (string).
- **Outputs and errors:** A string; no errors.
- **Side effects and interactions:** Pure function; no I/O. Depends on the package constants `GithubURI2` (`github://`), `GithubURI` (`github:`), and `HuggingFacePrefix` (`huggingface://`), whose exact string values the callers'"'"' prefix tests depend on.
- **Required sequencing and state:** The `github://` case is checked before the `github:` case (a `github://` input must not be misrouted to the `github:` branch); the huggingface case is independent. None of these cases produces side effects or state.
- **Region boundary:** Self-contained — the range spans the whole `ConvertURL` declaration from its `func` line through its closing brace.
```

Masked section 3:
```
- **Required interface:** `func DownloadFile(url string, filePath, sha string, fileN, total int, downloadStatus func(string, string, string, float64)) error` — exported, package-level, reached by `pkg/gallery.InstallModel`, `pkg/startup.PreloadModelsConfigurations`, and `core/config.BackendConfigLoader`. `func GetBase64Image(s string) (string, error)` — exported, package-level; no retained consumer at present, but it is part of the package'"'"'s exported surface.
- **Observable behavior:** `DownloadFile` downloads `url` to `filePath`, optionally verifying a SHA-256 digest. If `filePath` exists with a matching SHA the download is skipped; with a mismatching SHA the file is removed and re-downloaded; with no SHA an existing file is kept. The (converted) URL is fetched via HTTP GET; status >= 400 fails. The body is streamed into a temporary sibling file, hashed as it streams, with `downloadStatus` reporting progress; on success the temp file is renamed to `filePath`. When `sha` is set the streamed hash is compared. After a successful download, when `filePath` names an archive per `utils.IsArchive`, it is extracted into `filePath`'"'"'s directory via `utils.ExtractArchive`. `GetBase64Image` returns the base64 encoding of an `http`-prefixed URL'"'"'s body, strips a `data:image/jpeg;base64,` prefix, or returns `""` with error text `not valid string`.
- **Inputs:** `DownloadFile`: `url`, `filePath`, `sha` (optional digest; empty = none), `fileN`/`total` (multi-file progress scaling), `downloadStatus` (progress callback). `GetBase64Image`: `s` (string).
- **Outputs and errors:** `DownloadFile` returns `nil` on success or an error describing the failed step; callers check `err != nil`. `GetBase64Image` returns `(string, error)`; the `not valid string` error wording is the one consumed form. The `.partial` temporary sibling name and the SHA error wording are not externally consumed.
- **Side effects and interactions:** Writes `filePath` and a temporary sibling during streaming; may remove an existing `filePath` on SHA mismatch; creates parent directories; issues an HTTP GET; for archive destinations extracts into the parent directory. Uses `utils.IsArchive`/`utils.ExtractArchive` (cross-target `pkg/utils`).
- **Required sequencing and state:** URL conversion precedes the existence check; the existence/SHA check precedes fetch; parent-dir creation precedes streaming; the temp file is renamed only after a successful stream; SHA verification happens after rename; archive extraction happens after verification and only on success.
- **Region boundary:** Self-contained at the declaration level — the range spans two whole declarations (`DownloadFile` then `GetBase64Image`), each beginning at its `func` line and ending at its closing brace. However, the `DownloadFile` body references three names defined outside this region that the replacement must keep resolvable: `removePartialFile` (defined above this region in retained text), `calculateSHA` (defined below this region in retained text), and `progressWriter` (defined in `pkg/downloader/progress.go`). The replacement must continue to call these by those names or otherwise satisfy the retained references at the region'"'"'s last line; renaming them out of scope will not compile.
```

