This block states only where and how existing callers reach the implementation.
It does not state expected outcomes or prescribe implementation structure.

## Reached at
  An HTTP service at base URL http://localhost:8080, served by the
  /usr/local/bin/local-ai binary. The binary is built in the image from the Go
  source tree cloned into /app (module github.com/go-skynet/LocalAI, tag
  v2.15.0) via `make build`; the Go toolchain is retained in the image so the
  source under /app can be rebuilt after edits. The service process is started
  by /entrypoint.sh as:
      /usr/local/bin/local-ai --address 0.0.0.0:8080 --models-path /models
  with the environment variable MODELS_PATH=/models.

## Must provide
  GET    /readyz
  GET    /version
  GET    /models
  POST   /models/apply            accepts a JSON object body
  GET    /models/jobs
  GET    /models/jobs/{uuid}      {uuid} is a path segment
  GET    /models/galleries
  POST   /models/galleries         accepts a JSON object body
  DELETE /models/galleries         accepts a JSON object body
  GET    /models/available

## Called as
  GET /readyz
  GET /version
  GET /models
  POST /models/apply
    body: a JSON object. Fields a caller populates:
      url          string; functional callers pass a value of the form file://...
      id           string; functional callers pass a bare model id, or a value
                   of the form <gallery>@<model>
      config_url   string; functional callers pass a value of the form file://...
  GET /models/jobs
  GET /models/jobs/{uuid}
    uuid   a string path segment (the job identifier)
  GET /models/galleries
  POST /models/galleries
    body: a JSON object. Fields:
      name   string
      url    string; functional callers pass values of the form file://... or github:...
  DELETE /models/galleries
    body: a JSON object. Fields:
      name   string
  GET /models/available

## Setup required
  The service must be running and reachable at http://localhost:8080; the
  calling side polls GET /readyz until ready before issuing any other request.
  /models (the --models-path directory, MODELS_PATH=/models) is a shared,
  writable directory: the calling side writes files into it directly, and the
  service reads from it.
  Submissions to POST /models/apply are processed asynchronously; the calling
  side tracks each submission by its job identifier and polls
  GET /models/jobs/{uuid} with that identifier.

## Test harness boundary
  A pytest runner (launched via uv) runs in the same filesystem as the
  service: it polls GET /readyz for readiness, writes fixture files directly
  into /models, and issues HTTP requests to http://localhost:8080. That
  runner, its helper functions, and the fixture files it writes belong to the
  calling side, not to the implementation.
