- **Observable behavior:** The default content source for a tooltip. When a tooltip is opened for a target element, the widget calls the `content` function to obtain the text to render into the tooltip'"'"'s `.ui-tooltip-content` cell. The default implementation derives that content from the target element itself — from the value of the target'"'"'s `title` attribute. This is the mechanism by which a plain `$(el).attr("title", T).tooltip()` produces a tooltip whose content is the title text: at open time, the default `content` function reads that title attribute.
- **Inputs:** Implicit `this` — the target DOM element the tooltip describes (the element on which the tooltip is being opened; the retained code binds it via `.call( target[0], ... )`). One positional argument — a response callback function, provided by `_updateContent` for the async-response case; the default implementation ignores it.
- **Outputs and errors:** Returns the content to render. The retained code treats the return value as follows: a truthy return is passed synchronously to `_open(event, target, content)` and written into the tooltip content cell; a falsy return (e.g. when the target has no `title` attribute) causes `_open` to return without creating a tooltip. The return is a string when the target carries a `title` attribute, and falsy when it does not. The default does not throw.
- **Side effects and interactions:** None of its own beyond reading the target'"'"'s `title` attribute. Its return value drives the externally observable content of the generated tooltip element'"'"'s `.ui-tooltip-content` descendant (read by callers via `.text()` / `.html()`). The same value is what makes a tooltip open at all (falsy content suppresses creation). The retained open path has already stashed the original `title` under the `ui-tooltip-title` data key and cleared the attribute by the time `_open` writes content; the default reads the target'"'"'s `title` attribute at the moment `_updateContent` calls it, so the order in which the title is stashed/cleared relative to this call is established by the retained `_updateContent`/`_open` flow, not by this region.
- **Required sequencing and state:** The function is called during open (programmatic `tooltip("open")`, or a `mouseover`/`focusin` reaching the bound `open`), after the target is resolved via `closest(this.options.items)` and marked with `ui-tooltip-open`, and before `_open` creates the tooltip element. Its return value is consumed synchronously by the retained `_updateContent` (truthy → `_open`; falsy → no tooltip). The async response callback path (delivering content later through the callback argument) is part of the calling convention the retained code supports; the default does not use it, but a replacement default must still accept being called with the callback argument without error.
