## Reached at
  A browser-side jQuery UI widget, loaded by absolute `file://` path into a
  headless Chromium driven over Selenium. The program under test is the
  application'"'"'s own file staged by the image build at:
      /app/ui/jquery.ui.tooltip.js
  The harness page loads it together with its prerequisites straight from
  `/app` over `file://`, with no HTTP server in the observation path:
      <script src="file:///app/jquery-1.8.3.js"></script>
      <script src="file:///app/ui/jquery.ui.core.js"></script>
      <script src="file:///app/ui/jquery.ui.widget.js"></script>
      <script src="file:///app/ui/jquery.ui.position.js"></script>
      <script src="file:///app/ui/jquery.ui.tooltip.js"></script>
  Callers reach the widget by executing inline JavaScript through
  `driver.execute_script(...)` against the loaded document.

## Must provide
  `jQuery.fn.tooltip`            function, registered by `$.widget("ui.tooltip", { ... })`
                                 in /app/ui/jquery.ui.tooltip.js; the constructor
                                 (`$(...).tooltip()`) and the string-method form
                                 (`$(...).tooltip("<method>")`) must both resolve.
  Widget method `"open"`         opens/renders the tooltip for the element.
  Widget method `"close"`        closes an open tooltip.
  Widget method `"destroy"`      tears down the widget for the element.
  Event-driven open              `mouseover` and `focusin` on an initialised
                                 element must reach the same open path.
  `ui-tooltip-id` data key       set on the target element so a caller can look
                                 up the generated tooltip by id.
  `.ui-tooltip-content` element  a descendant of the generated tooltip that
                                 callers read (`.text()` / `.html()`).
  Generated tooltip element      a `<div id="ui-tooltip-N" ...>` appended to the
                                 document body, addressable by `jQuery("#" + id)`.

## Called as
  Initialize on an element:
      jQuery("<span>...</span>").attr("title", <string>).appendTo("body").tooltip()
      jQuery("<input>").attr("title", <string>).appendTo("body").tooltip()
    `title` — set via `.attr("title", ...)`, a string; supplied to the page as
    `arguments[0]` of `driver.execute_script`.

  Programmatic open:
      elem.tooltip().tooltip("open")
    `"open"` — 1st positional argument to the widget method call; a string.

  Mouseover entry point:
      elem[0].dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent("mouseover", {bubbles: true, cancelable: true}))

  Focusin entry point:
      elem[0].focus()

  Close / destroy:
      elem.tooltip("close")
      elem.tooltip("destroy")
    `"close"` / `"destroy"` — 1st positional argument; a string.

  State a caller reads (observation hooks, not results):
      elem.data("ui-tooltip-id")
      jQuery("#" + id)
      tip.find(".ui-tooltip-content").text()
      tip.find(".ui-tooltip-content").html()
      tip.is(":visible")
      tip.offset()  /  elem.offset()
      jQuery("#" + id).length

## Setup required
  The `/app` tree must exist and be readable, staged by the image build:
  `jquery-1.8.3.js`, `ui/jquery.ui.{core,widget,position,tooltip}.js`, and
  `themes/base/jquery.ui.all.css` under `/app`.
  A genuine headless Chromium binary and `/usr/bin/chromedriver` (real ELF
  executables of realistic size, not wrapper scripts) must be present; the
  calling-side runner refuses anything smaller or non-ELF.
  Chromium is launched with `--headless`, `--no-sandbox`,
  `--disable-dev-shm-usage`, `--disable-gpu`, `--allow-file-access-from-files`
  (so `file://` URLs are readable through the browser'"'"'s own stack), and
  `--window-size=1920,1080`; page-load timeout 30s.
  The calling-side runner materializes a fresh harness page at a per-run path
  under `/tmp` from a suite-owned template, substituting a fresh marker token,
  and exports `HARNESS_URL`, `HARNESS_MARKER`, and `ATTACK_TOKEN` into the
  environment before invoking pytest. Each test begins by loading that
  harness page, which asserts its own marker and that `jQuery` and
  `jQuery.fn.tooltip` are `function` before any probe runs.

## Test harness boundary
  The calling side — not part of the implementation and not to be rebuilt —
  consists of: a pytest runner invoked through `uv`; a Selenium `webdriver`
  driving the headless Chromium/chromedriver binaries; a suite-owned harness
  HTML page materialized at a per-run `/tmp` path with a fresh marker token
  that loads only the application'"'"'s own `/app` files over `file://` and
  contributes no application logic of its own; and the inline JavaScript
  strings passed to `driver.execute_script` that drive and observe the
  widget. These are the means of reaching the target; the target is the
  application'"'"'s own widget file under `/app`.
