## Reached at
  OpenJPEG 2.2.0, staged by the image build with its source tree at
  /app/openjpeg-2.2.0 and installed under /usr/local. Callers reach the TGA
  loader by two routes, and both terminate in the same project-owned code:

  1. Installed CLI binary, spawned through subprocess with absolute paths:
         /usr/local/bin/opj_compress -i <input_path> -o <output_path>
     The binary is the project'"'"'s own build output (cmake + make install from
     /app/openjpeg-2.2.0/build). The caller verifies the file at that path is
     a native ELF executable and is executable; a wrapper script in its place
     is refused. opj_compress selects the input decoder from the file
     extension of the -i argument; a .tga extension dispatches to the
     project'"'"'s TGA loader, tgatoimage, inside src/bin/jp2/opj_compress.c.
  2. A caller-side consumer process compiled fresh on every run by gcc from an
     embedded C main plus the project'"'"'s own translation unit
         /app/openjpeg-2.2.0/src/bin/jp2/convert.c
     linked against the project'"'"'s libopenjp2, calling the loader directly as
     declared in src/bin/jp2/convert.h:
         opj_image_t *image = tgatoimage(argv[1], &parameters);

  A sibling installed tool, /usr/local/bin/opj_decompress, is also spawned by
  absolute path to decode a produced codestream. It is a retained binary from
  the same project build that callers require to be present; it is not the
  site being reconstructed.

